  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA_n2000, avgpool) achieved the best accuracy so far (0.591), a substantial +10.6% jump over single-profile PCA (0.485), confirming multi-profile is the most impactful design choice. RNA clearly dominates image (0.485 vs 0.208). Uncertainty: whether transformer aggregation can further improve over avgpool for multi-profile RNA. This experiment (config_003) isolates the aggregation variable by comparing transformer vs avgpool with the same RNA encoder (PCA_n2000) and multi-profile setting, directly extending the best result. It is the best use of this slot because it is a clean single-variable comparison that either confirms avgpool as the best aggregation or reveals a further gain, and the outcome will inform the aggregation choice for subsequent multimodal fusion experiments (configs 018-021, 024-027) where aggregation is also a critical design axis. With 5 experiments remaining, establishing the optimal aggregation now maximizes the value of later multimodal trials."
